+## Keys and roles
+
+Every request sends `Authorization: Bearer <key>`. Keys are stored in the
+data (`apiKeys`, see `docs/DATA.md`). Without a key, or with a key that is
+not known, the answer is 401 `unauthorized`. A known key whose role may not
+use the route gets 403 `forbidden`.
+
+- `viewer`: every `GET` route except `GET /audit`.
+- `cook`: as viewer, plus `POST /recipes/:id/cook`, `POST /batches/:id/waste`,
+  `POST /temperatures` and `POST /stocktakes/:id/counts`.
+- `manager`: every route, including `GET /audit`.
+
+## Audit
+
+Every request with a known key that may change data (any method but `GET`)
+writes an audit entry `{ id, at, keyName, method, path, status }`, also when
+it is refused or fails. `GET /audit` lists the entries newest first
+(managers only).
+
